        "parms": "1. Play a key on a keyboard at port 0. midiin sends three ints, and its box shows the last: the velocity. xmidiin sends the three as one list. Let go and the list starts with 128, a note-off, or 144 with velocity 0: keyboards use either.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
      "object 19": {
        "ID": 19,
        "gui": {
          "x": "640.0",
          "y": "340.0",
          "w": "300"
        },
        "parms": "2. No keyboard? Feed midiparse by hand: click 144, 60 and 100 in turn. The third byte completes a note-on, and the note box shows 60 100. The channel box, second from the right, shows 1: the low four bits of the status byte, counted from 1.",
        "type": ".text"
      },
